   "three-pass history: (1) literature research cross-verified LDG 1998 primary
    (gr-qc/0405033) + independent author Francis-Kosowsky (gr-qc/0311007) on the
    vacuum action, Omega-field equation (eq 4.37/4.40), closed-form solution
    (eq 4.49-4.53), and LDG's own Schwarzschild worked example (eq 6.79/6.73);
    (2) a first standalone numeric verification FAILED and correctly diagnosed
    why -- pdftotext extraction of eq 4.28/4.49-4.53 was garbled, AND the wrong
    covariant derivative was used (Phase 0a's flat rotation-gauge-only D_mu
    instead of the calligraphic D from Table 2 using hbar(grad) and
    omega(a)=Omega(h(a))) -- reusing the wrong operator builds a teleparallel
    connection with IDENTICALLY ZERO curvature by construction, a structurally
    wrong equation not a sign slip; (3) reading actual PDF PAGE IMAGES (not text
    extraction) resolved this, and a standalone Python/numpy verification
    reproduced LDG's closed-form Schwarzschild curvature (eq 6.73) to ~1e-13,
    Ricci=0 to 1e-17 to 1e-19 at 3 points -- clearing ADR-2607102300's
    verification bar, independently re-run and confirmed by the requester before
    Clojure implementation began"
   "Clojure port (PR #9) landed: frame-adjoint (eq 2.46, self-inverse h<->hbar
    adjoint), minimal new GA primitives on existing kotoba.sm.tensor
    (bivector<->matrix, wedge-vectors, vector-dot-bivector, bivector-commutator,
    outermorphism -- no from-scratch GA engine), H-field+omega-from-h (eq
    4.49/4.53, vacuum spin-free closed-form Omega(h)), L-a-omega+riemann-basis-pair
    +riemann-map-matrix+riemann-map (eq 4.48, the COVARIANT Riemann map using
    position-gauge-covariant L_a, not Phase 0a's flat derivative), curvature-scalar
    (true LDG Ricci scalar R=sum_ab gamma^a.(gamma^b.R(h_b^h_a)), using the FIXED
    background frame's own trivial reciprocal per Phase 0d's 2-source literature
    finding -- reachable only because riemann-map supplies the previously-missing
    bilinear extension to general bivectors)"
   "before merge, requester independently re-derived Schwarzschild regression
    numbers in a live Clojure REPL session -- caught and corrected a mistake in
    that independent re-derivation itself (forgot the hbar->h frame-adjoint
    conversion on first attempt, giving spuriously near-zero results), landing
    on values matching committed tests to the same tolerance after correction"
   "verification landed WITH the code: Schwarzschild regression at 2 independent
    points/masses (error ~1e-9 to 1e-10, within FD tolerance), curvature-scalar
    approx 0 at both (expected vacuum result) and EXACTLY 0.0 at flat limit
    (h=position-gauge-identity, every derivative vanishes identically)"
   "QUALITATIVE SCOPE CHANGE from every prior ADR: ADR-2607051500 through
    ADR-2607101900 all framed this repo as classical field algebra only, NOT an
    action/field-equation engine -- that framing no longer fully applies, this
    repo now contains a genuine field EQUATION (vacuum Omega(h)) and its
    physical consequence (curvature scalar verified against an exact solution).
    What has NOT changed: still bounded to vacuum/spin-free, verified against
    exactly ONE exact solution (Schwarzschild) not a general GR-equivalence
    proof, and every ADR-2607102300 boundary (matter coupling, Einstein
    multivector/stress-energy sourcing i.e. non-vacuum G(a)=kappa*T(a),
    spin/torsion via full eq 4.28, quantization/RGE/scattering/lattice,
    dark-sector/de-Sitter) remains out of scope, not implicitly widened"
   "methodological note: this is the SECOND time in this repo's history (after
    PR #6's self-interaction-term slot-order bug) that a seemingly-thorough
    single pass produced a confidently-wrong result that failed SILENTLY
    (identically-zero curvature, no error thrown) rather than loudly -- caught
    only because the success criterion was an independent numeric match against
    a known closed-form result, not merely 'does the code run' or 'does the
    formula resemble the paper'. Not license to relax this discipline for
    future phases."]
